'AI re-drove the datasheet path for the rows that previously had engine evidence only, drove the datasheet Save Record action to capture Access own validation text, selected the screenshots to publish, and drafted this amendment entry. The auditor read every captured string against the earlier engine string and against the blueprint before accepting it.',
'Revision of the M7 audit report after the first push: widen the datasheet evidence and publish the relationship and dialog screenshots inside the repository.',
'The first push reported 46/46 PASS but labelled most rule rows as engine-only. The workbook instructs edit-in-Datasheet-View, commit, reopen and record; an all-engine report would under-deliver that. The datasheet Save Record action turned out to raise Access own validation text for rule and required fields, so ten rows were re-driven that way and their Method column now names the datasheet track. The 11 referential-integrity rows could not be re-driven (their dialog only fires when the grid leaves the dirty row, keyboard stays inside the row, Save Record returns an unrelated command error, hand-driven clicking locked the mouse), so they stay engine-labelled instead of being restated as UI observations.',
